## 🎯 Why use Channels?

| Benefit | Go (native) | TS (simulated) |
|---------|--------------|----------------|
| **Back‑pressure** – buffers fill up when downstream is slower. | Built‑in buffer size, `close` semantics. | Manual control via length checks; can replace with a proper queue library if needed. |
| **Decoupling** – producers and consumers evolve independently (e.g., add new stages). | Add another consumer channel without touching existing code. | Use additional async functions that read from the same buffer. |
| **Safety** – prevents uncontrolled memory growth when buffers are bounded. | Compiler enforces capacity checks (`make(chan T, n)`). | Manual length checks + `Array.shift()` prevent accidental overflow (but runtime error if not guarded). |

