  ### How it works  
  
  | Step | What happens |
  |------|--------------|
  | **Initialization** (`new BloomFilter(expectedItems, fpRate)`) | Computes optimal number of bits `m` and hash count `k`. Uses the classic formula:<br>`m = -n * ln(p) / (ln2²)`<br>`k = ceil(-ln(p) * n / m)` |
  | **Add** (`add(item)`) | Runs `k` independent Murmur3‑style hashes, maps each hash to a bit index modulo `m`, and sets that bit. |
  | **Has** (`has(item)`) | Same hashing; if any bit is 0 the item *cannot* be present → returns `false`. If all bits are set it returns `true` (a possible false positive). |
  | **JSON serialization** | The filter can be persisted as `{size, k, bitsBase64}` – only a few dozen bytes even for millions of items. |
  
