Below are three **complete**, self‑contained implementations of a simple *thread‑safe* in‑memory message queue that supports:

| Operation | Description |
|-----------|-------------|
| `enqueue(item)` / `push(item)` | Add an item to the back (tail) of the queue. |
| `dequeue()` / `pop()` | Remove and return the front (head) item, or throw if empty. |
| `peek()` / `front()` | Return the front item **without** removing it, or throw if empty. |

All three languages use a lock‑based approach (`Mutex`/`sync.Mutex`/`sync.RWMutex`) so that concurrent callers can safely call these methods from multiple goroutines (Go), threads (Python) and JavaScript workers (TypeScript).  

