## ✅ Quick Checklist for Production

| Item | Why it matters |
|------|----------------|
| **Strong random generator** (≥256 bits) | Prevents brute‑force guessing of the verifier. |
| **URL‑safe Base64 without padding** (`-` `_`) | Guarantees URL safety and avoids extra `=` characters that could be stripped by some libraries. |
| **Exact match verification** (`===` / `==`) | PKCE mandates no tolerance for case, whitespace or padding differences. |
| **Store verifier securely (e.g., short‑lived DB entry)** | The server must retain the exact verifier until the auth code is exchanged; otherwise replay attacks are possible. |
| **Validate challenge method header** (`S256`) on the authorization request | Guarantees that the client actually performed PKCE and didn’t fall back to plain `code_challenge=plain`. |

