| Step | What happens |
|------|--------------|
| **Chunking** | The number is repeatedly divided by 1000, extracting the lowest three‑digit “chunk”. Each chunk (< 1000) is turned into words via `helperThree`. |
| **Helper logic** | Handles units (1‑9), teens (10‑19), and normal tens (20,30,…). If a hundred exists it appends *“hundred”* followed by the remainder. |
| **Scale labels** | The appropriate scale word (`thousand`, `million`, …) is inserted between chunks. |
| **Assembly** | Pieces are concatenated with spaces; leading/trailing whitespace is trimmed before returning. |

