### How it works

| Step | What happens |
|------|--------------|
| **Enqueue** (`enqueue`) | Adds a task to the shared `tasks` array and updates `lastTaskTime`. If depth > `maxDepth`, `_maybeAddWorker()` is invoked. |
| **Scaling up** | `_maybeAddWorker()` spawns a new `worker_threads.Worker` (the same file, so each worker runs in its own thread). Workers forward any received message back to the main process via `onMessage`. The optional metric callback lets you log or display current depth/worker count. |
| **Scaling down** | `_removeIdleWorkers()` checks how long it’s been since the last task arrived and terminates workers once they’ve been idle longer than `idleTimeoutMs`. If a worker dies while all other workers are also idle, the pool will spawn another one to keep at least `minWorkers` alive. |
| **Shutdown** | Call `pool.shutdown()` (e.g., on SIGINT) – it safely terminates every worker and waits for them to exit before exiting itself. |

